IMPORT prelude
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC, phase 1 (front end): the barrier form.
--
-- Every tenant must sign. `ONCE ALL HAVE` is the barrier (R-Q1, RULED
-- 2026-09-07): HENCE fires ONCE, when the last of them has signed (spec
-- §2.2.6, §3.1). LEST fires at the deadline, and blames exactly the tenants
-- who did not sign (§6.1). The ONCE line is mandatory whenever an EVERY has a
-- HENCE or a LEST; see not-ok/tc/every-continuation-without-join.l4.
--
-- This file is the FRONT END's witness: it shows the shape. The #EVAL at the
-- foot has no event stream, so what it prints is the rule itself, unarmed and
-- with its cast not yet drawn. Running one against events is run-barrier.l4.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Deliver HAS who    IS AN Actor, what IS A STRING

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the tenancy begins` MEANS
    PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) what WITHIN 5

-- `EVERY Tenant t`: the pattern form (RULED 2026-09-07). `Tenant` is a
-- constructor of `Actor`, not a type; it selects the cast. `t` is bound to
-- each member, at type Actor, in the action, the deadline, HENCE and LEST.
--
-- `Sign (EXACTLY t)`, not `Sign t`: an action is a pattern, and a bare `t`
-- there would be a NEW name matching any signer. EXACTLY makes it the member.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`all tenants sign` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  `the tenancy begins`
        LEST   BREACH

#EVAL `all tenants sign`
